---
/**
 * Day 0 — the run itself.
 *
 * These four bands are the `stacktape init` wizard's own, imported rather than rewritten. That is
 * the point: the wizard's argument — nothing leaves your machine, nothing is billed yet, every
 * choice cites the line of your code that caused it — is already the strongest thing this page can
 * say, and marketing copy paraphrasing it would only make it weaker and less true.
 *
 * So this file adds almost no words. It supplies the anchors the rail needs, one beat between the
 * review and the deploy, and the Review band's diagram at the size the diagram deserves.
 *
 * `InitWizardRun.astro` is not used as a whole because it brings its own masthead and its own rail,
 * and this page already has a rail that spans both days. The bands are exported individually for
 * exactly this reason.
 *
 * The diagram is `client:only` — its icon pack cannot be prerendered — so its canvas keeps a fixed
 * height and nothing on the page moves when the island arrives.
 */
import { ACME_DIAGRAM_CONFIG } from '../../surfaces/InitWizardRun/acme-config';
import { AnalyzeBand, DeployBand, ReviewDetails, ReviewIntro, StartBand } from '../../surfaces/InitWizardRun/bands';
import DiagramIsland from '../../surfaces/InitWizardRun/DiagramIsland';
import { DeployTerminal } from '../../surfaces/DeployTerminal';
---

<section class="a-day">
  <div class="a-daymark a-daymark--first">
    <p class="a-daymark__tag">Day 0</p>
    <h2 class="a-daymark__title">The first hour</h2>
    <p class="a-daymark__lede">
      You have a repository and an AWS account. Nothing else is set up. This is what one command does with that, in
      order — and nothing exists on AWS until the last step.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="a-band" id="start">
    <StartBand />
  </div>

  <div class="a-band" id="analyze">
    <AnalyzeBand />
  </div>

  <section class="wizard-band a-band" id="review">
    <ReviewIntro />

    <div class="wizard-diagram a-diagram">
      <div class="wizard-diagram__views">
        <span class="wizard-diagram__view is-active">Diagram</span>
        <span class="wizard-diagram__view">What &amp; why</span>
        <span class="wizard-diagram__view">stacktape.yml</span>
      </div>
      <div class="wizard-diagram__canvas a-diagram__canvas">
        <DiagramIsland
          client:only="react"
          ariaLabel="Diagram of the infrastructure this configuration creates"
          config={ACME_DIAGRAM_CONFIG}
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="a-caption a-caption--between">
      Six resources, and the 33 CloudFormation resources it takes to run them safely. This is the same diagram the
      Console draws once the stack exists — it is not a picture made for this page.
    </p>

    <ReviewDetails />
  </section>

  <section class="a-band" id="deploy">
    <p class="a-beat">You press Deploy. From here it is CloudFormation, and it tells you what it is doing.</p>

    <DeployTerminal />

    <p class="a-caption">
      The real transcript: phases, the change summary CloudFormation returned, and which resources are still being
      created. Packaging your code runs about <strong>7× faster</strong> than the same project through CDK.
    </p>

    <div class="a-surface">
      <DeployBand />
    </div>
  </section>
</section>
